72 712 Td (Project Report: Autonomous Optical Waste Sorting Robot) Tj
0 -20 Td (Authors: Robotics & Mechatronics Engineering Senior Design) Tj
0 -30 Td (1. Problem Definition:) Tj
0 -15 Td (Municipal recycling facilities face high labor costs and 35% manual error rate in waste separation.) Tj
0 -15 Td (This project builds an automated optical sorter using computer vision to classify plastics and metals.) Tj
0 -30 Td (2. Technical Methodology:) Tj
0 -15 Td (We integrated a YOLOv8-nano neural network on an NVIDIA Jetson Nano controller.) Tj
0 -15 Td (High-resolution industrial camera captures items at 60 fps on a conveyor belt.) Tj
0 -30 Td (3. Implementation and Evidence:) Tj
0 -15 Td (Pneumatic actuators divert non-recyclable materials in 45 milliseconds.) Tj
0 -15 Td (Hardware prototype built with aluminum framing and stepper motor-driven belt.) Tj
0 -30 Td (4. Innovation:) Tj
0 -15 Td (Custom multi-spectral lighting system distinguishes clear PET from HDPE plastics under ambient light.) Tj
0 -30 Td (5. Testing and Validation:) Tj
0 -15 Td (Tested across 2,500 samples: achieved 96.4% sorting accuracy and 120 items/minute throughput.) Tj
0 -30 Td (6. Documentation and Reproducibility:) Tj
0 -15 Td (Full CAD schematics, bill of materials ( total), and Docker container available on GitHub.) Tj
